msgid "Base fill price resolved on the fill bar."
msgstr ""

#: 1db9afa404d04626981991ee243aa809 of pybroker.slippage.SlippageContext:29
msgid ""
"Column scope over the whole test window — **not** pre-sliced to the fill "
"bar. Causal reads must bound every fetch with the fill bar's index, e.g. "
"``ctx.col_scope.fetch(ctx.symbol, \"close\", "
"end_index=ctx.sym_end_index[ctx.symbol])``; fetching without "
"``end_index`` returns the full window, including bars after the fill. "
"``None`` when bar data is unavailable, in which case volume- and "
"volatility-based models leave the fill unadjusted."
msgstr ""

#: 767270bf5a7648eda14fce64a9231828 of pybroker.slippage.SlippageContext:38
msgid "pybroker.scope.ColumnScope | None"
msgstr ""

#: a7a8a3754faa45a69059da648e6fe43c of pybroker.slippage.SlippageContext:42
msgid ""
"Indicator scope over the whole test window — the same ``end_index`` bound"
" applies as for ``col_scope``. ``None`` when indicator data is "
"unavailable, in which case indicator-based models leave the fill "
"unadjusted."
msgstr ""

#: 5e2732b3b62f43e2a3117495bc9717c0 of pybroker.slippage.SlippageContext:47
msgid "pybroker.scope.IndicatorScope | None"
msgstr ""

#: 221ee2fe471341b58d176b241675f120 of pybroker.slippage.SlippageContext:51
msgid "Current bar index per symbol, or ``None`` when unavailable."
msgstr ""

#: b0be0c10ec9b4e6a8033c0acfb8a486c of pybroker.slippage.SlippageContext:54
msgid "Mapping[str, int] | None"
msgstr ""

#: 91e12bd509d8491bb205c09dd005fb8c of pybroker.slippage.SlippageContext:58
msgid ""
"Whether fractional shares are enabled. When ``False``, a returned share "
"quantity is truncated to a whole number by the caller; the flag lets a "
"model compute price-dependent values (such as volume participation) from "
"the quantity that will actually fill."
msgstr ""

#: 8da2fcb433704f24b4bb9f8dd7513f1a of pybroker.slippage.SlippageContext:64
msgid "bool"
msgstr ""

#: 90b96bbbe4574d0883fce1b1a41ea082 of pybroker.slippage.SlippageModel:1
msgid "Base class for implementing a slippage model."
msgstr ""

#: a60855520c4a42de8de0c9e03d558373 of pybroker.slippage.SlippageModel:3
msgid ""
"A slippage model may adjust fill price, share quantity, or both, using "
"data from the fill bar in :meth:`apply_slippage`."
msgstr ""

#: df04aa092ff04bc9afbb1f3417133dc9 of pybroker.slippage.SlippageModel:6
msgid ""
":meth:`apply_slippage` is called for scheduled buy and sell orders, for "
"stop exits (stop loss, take profit, trailing, and bar stops), and for "
":meth:`pybroker.portfolio.Portfolio.exit_position` fills. Stop and exit "
"fills apply the returned **fill price only**; a returned share quantity "
"is ignored, since those paths exit an entry in full."
msgstr ""

#: f6bfdaa477aa4427b9fa7558c7dd5529 of
#: pybroker.slippage.SlippageModel.adjust_fill:1
msgid ""
"Builds a :class:`.SlippageContext` and applies :meth:`apply_slippage` to "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: 8e8187d1329e450eb21e286a480fd07e of
#: pybroker.slippage.SlippageModel.adjust_fill:4
msgid ""
"Provided so that callers which cannot import :mod:`pybroker.slippage` "
"(such as :mod:`pybroker.portfolio`) can still apply slippage to a fill."
msgstr ""

#: 056d736a41d84ffc860ce588cb969cc3 605b10a3b59c41e78e968aa76e93d9ad of
#: pybroker.slippage.SlippageModel.validate:1
#: pybroker.slippage.VolumeSlippageModel.validate:1
msgid "Validates model configuration before a backtest starts."
msgstr ""

#: ff5b8709c3f54af1b707611be5803037 of
#: pybroker.slippage.VolatilitySlippageModel:1
msgid "ATR-scaled slippage on fill price."
msgstr ""

#: 8ba99a706cdd44c689e6c2d8708fa568 of
#: pybroker.slippage.VolatilitySlippageModel:3
msgid ""
"Adverse price adjustment equals ``scale * ATR`` at the fill bar, where "
"the Average True Range is computed over the ``atr_period`` bars ending at"
" the fill bar (see :func:`pybroker.vect.atr`). Fills during the warmup "
"period -- the first ``atr_period`` bars, which have no full ATR window --"
" or on bars where the ATR is ``NaN`` are left unadjusted."
msgstr ""

#: 45ed4893bde14f01bb531a9bfe2952b8 of
#: pybroker.slippage.VolatilitySlippageModel:9
msgid "Number of lookback bars for the ATR. Defaults to ``14``."
msgstr ""

#: 0a67d72ef83f4887ae7ec4f55ea1e77a of
#: pybroker.slippage.VolatilitySlippageModel:10
msgid "Multiplier applied to the ATR value."
msgstr ""

#: 3e9026e7b0b94c2b93c3f0d03b989545 of pybroker.slippage.VolumeSlippageModel:1
msgid "Volume-based participation cap and square-law price impact."
msgstr ""

#: 34a2c876dfc149e2973a1decac5b461a of pybroker.slippage.VolumeSlippageModel:3
msgid ""
"Share quantity may be capped at ``volume_limit * bar_volume``. Price "
"impact is ``price_impact * (filled_shares / bar_volume) ** 2``. Either "
"effect can be disabled by passing ``0`` or ``None``."
msgstr ""

#: 891cce73e66a4f22b40a7f2eac33827f of pybroker.slippage.VolumeSlippageModel:7
msgid ""
"Requires a ``volume`` data column, which is optional in PyBroker. Bars "
"where the volume is missing or ``NaN`` are left unadjusted."
msgstr ""

#: 507aeabc5d8442bba0e39ea55617b8f3 of pybroker.slippage.VolumeSlippageModel:10
msgid "Square-law impact coefficient. ``0`` disables impact."
msgstr ""

#: 0d74eadd66d84ccaa81fff9a52f086f6 of pybroker.slippage.VolumeSlippageModel:11
msgid ""
"Max participation as a fraction of bar volume. ``None`` or ``0`` disables"
" the cap."
msgstr ""

